  that's when i started my youtube channel  and my official website a few months  into copid  i got a job offer from a company that i  was really interested in  and they had like a four-step interview  process and in the end what got me the  offer was my videos apparently during  the interview process one of the  partners thought i was a little  dry  um i don't know what that means but  maybe i was being too didactic maybe i  was nervous maybe i was trying to keep  it too like professional  um but after they had watched my videos  they kind of warmed up to me and  came through with an offer i think it's  almost like getting a second chance to  make a good impression  like it makes them feel like they know  you a little better you guys have  probably heard the statistic before but  like something like 70  of your interviewers are gonna google  you before they interview  and most firms these days they're  looking for people  um yeah to do the drawings and to do the  work but they're also looking for the  right fit  and for people who can make a meaningful  contribution to the firm when i went  into the interviews like almost everyone  knew about my videos which was  actually a little weird  but also cool because it gave them a  sense of like my interests and my  passions and what i'm into  um and it gives them a sense of like who  i am as a person before like ah me going  into trying to explain it to them of  course getting a job isn't the only  benefit of having an online presence it  can also help you establish yourself as  an expert in a topic  um on a personal level it can force you  to build expertise in a topic  it can help you make side income  it can help you make friends and meet  other people who have the same interests  and it can also get you raving fans  now i am not saying that you need to go  and make a youtube channel  in fact if you're in school you probably  want to use that time to focus on school  because this stuff is a lot of work  what i'm saying is like having some sort  of personal professional content online  that gives people a sense of who you are  and what your passions are  and like what you're knowledgeable in  can give you a competitive edge when  you're looking for a job  now architects by nature are generalists  so you could start a vlog and talk about  whatever your interests are from day to  day but we don't have an unlimited  amount of time in the day so you kind of  want this content to be as effective as  possible so if i were you um i would try  to develop a niche in one or two topics  i think that would be more beneficial  than doing something general but you  might be thinking uh but i don't really  have an expertise in anything  no problem  you can build expertise  that's literally what i did when i was  in my uh little slump  um i sat down and i asked these four  questions  uh what am i good at  uh what are my interests  what do i enjoy doing  what do other people say i'm good at and  do i have any proven accomplishments  you take the combination of that  and you don't have to  start off as an expert nobody is the  whole fun part is that through the  process of researching writing and  talking about it you are teaching  yourself  and slowly you are becoming someone  people can refer to the best part about  this creating educational content online  is not  the raging fans uh although i do really  appreciate you guys  it's not even the monetization  although i do love money  like forget about the jobs or the  monetization like it's really about me  and like helping me become a better  communicator  it is so true what they say like the  best way to learn something is to teach  it to other people  and when you can distill down ideas and  break it down in simple terms for other  people to understand  um and for other people to use  like you're learning so much more  through that process and i think that is  priceless  and that is something that not a lot of  courses can teach you  so one of